title: "Evidence-Bound Adversarial Verification (EBAV): A Governed Field Method for AI-Assisted Software Verification and Release"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Coleman
    given-names: Brendon R.
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-13
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://brendonrcoleman.com/methods/ebav/"
abstract: >-
  A proposed seven-stage method combining immutable candidate preservation,
  adversarial review, regression-driven remediation, evidence-bounded claims,
  and separately scoped human authorization for AI-assisted software releases.
keywords:
  - adversarial software verification
  - AI-assisted software engineering
  - release governance
  - provenance
  - mutation testing
  - software supply chain
